I've written the assessment to session_plan/assessment.md, but it isn't committed. session_plan/ is gitignored, so the instructed git add … || true does nothing. I force-added it by mistake, then undid that unpushed commit, so the tree is back at 648861af with the file on disk for the planner.

Main findings:

1. The MCP half of #1064 is ready to build. @yuanhao's decision on the ticket: "scrub MCP stdio servers by default too, like hooks," with YOYO_SUBPROCESS_ENV_SCRUB=0 still turning it off. He also posted the API and a test recipe. The yoagent version that adds the API (0.26.8) is now in Cargo.lock. One function, mcp_prefix::mcp_stdio_options(), is used by both server launches (the pre-flight check and the real connect), and subprocess_env::hook_scrub_vars() already has the fail-closed gate hooks use. Today yoyo passes every provider API key it inherits to every MCP server.

2. New bug, reproduced, not filed: yoyo thinks ast-grep is installed when it isn't. On this runner /usr/bin/sg is util-linux's set-group command. It exits 0 on --version, so the availability check passes.
   • yoyo ast foo fails with sg: unrecognized option '--pattern' instead of saying ast-grep is missing.
   • yoyo map --all reports "(using ast-grep)" while every file falls back to regex.
   • test_ast_grep_search_no_sg never asserts anything on this runner.

   ast-grep's maintainer also started retiring the sg name in July 2026, so yoyo will break for real ast-grep users too. The fix is to prefer the ast-grep binary and accept sg only if its version text names ast-grep. I saved this to yopedia.

3. #1111's class still has three misreads. I probed all 39 shell commands with --bogus. Three still treat it as an argument:
   • ast searches for the pattern "--bogus".
   • blame passes it to git blame, which then errors.
   • test ignores it and carries on.

   #1111 is closed, so these have no open ticket.

4. Other notes:
   • All recent runs are green with no reverts.
   • The "prompt" area took 5 of the last 10 self-driven changes, which argues against #1126 for that slot.
   • src/config.rs is 11 lines from failing the module size test.
   • Claude Code 2.1.317 (released today) made the same unset-not-empty fix for MCP server environments.
